// Ch15 B15 "The ship" (C, 1 min). H16: the next dawn; a Hollowmere ship (a lashed double hull, tide-wheels,
// two windmills) readied to carry the party south as far as the shallows allow and wait at the Rim (ADR
// 0016: a chosen voyage after grief among allies). Liss aboard first with the cracked lamp in a padded box.
// Kerrid last up the gangway, as on a stair. One line from the dock-master; "it" stays ambiguous.
title: ch15_the_ship
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
@letterbox on
@camera H16
@mark liss ship_deck_1 walk
@wait 2.0
@anim aldous_varrow look_at liss
Aldous_varrow as "Dock-master" [neutral]: Bring it back. #line:ch15_ship_001 #tn:"Deliberately ambiguous: the lamp, the ship, or herself."
@mark toma ship_deck_2 walk
@mark asha ship_deck_3 walk
@mark rhen ship_deck_4 walk
@wait 2.0
@mark kerrid ship_deck_5 walk
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch15_complete = true>>
@fade out 2.0
@letterbox off
===
